The code comes from the CGP example of [epita_ani3d_lab_code-2027](https://github.com/drohmer/epita_ani3d_lab_code-2027)
(`examples/02_marching_cubes/02_marching_cube_dynamic`).

## What is new

- **ImGui readable on the projector:** `?gui_scale=1.4` enlarges its text, through `project::gui_scale`, which the
  template of CGP gives to ImGui at each frame. Its sections stay closed at start: a long window goes out of the
  frame.
- **The same variables for ImGui and the slide:** they are declared to the bridge, with what to recompute when
  the slide changes them. ImGui shows the new values at the next frame, as it reads them.
- **Two controls hidden on the web:** the wireframe (`glPolygonMode`, see [example 4](../05_buttons/index.html))
  and the export of the mesh to a file, which would land in the memory of the page.
- **Mouse:** in CGP, ImGui takes the clicks over its window; elsewhere the mouse turns the camera.

